      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults, and most regimens stay at or below 2,400 mg/day. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. Possible intended regimens include:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the absolute ceiling, generally for short-term use)\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also add a note with your rationale to the order."
      }
     ],
